g gives the estimated depth of the seal, gt^h , in meters, t minutes after the seal enters the water. It’s given that function g estimates that the seal reached its maximum depth of .3024 meters 6 minutes after it entered the water. Therefore, function g can be expressed in vertex form as .gt at 63 02 42=- +^^hh , where a is a constant. Since it’s also given that the seal reached the surface of the water after 12 minutes, g 12 0=^h . Substituting 12 for t and 0 for gt^h in .gt at 63 02 42=- +^^hh yields .a01 26 30242=- +^h , or .a36 3024=- . Dividing both sides of this equation by 36 gives .a 84=- . Substituting .84- for a in .gt at 63 02 42=- +^^hh gives ..gt t84 63 02 42=- -+^^hh . Substituting 10 for t in gt^h gives ..g 10 84 10 63 02 42=- -+^^ hh , which is equivalent to ..g 10 84 43 02 42=- +^^ hh , or g 10 168=^h . Therefore, the estimated depth, to the nearest meter, of the seal 10 minutes after it entered the water was 168 meters.","figurePath":"assets/sat-practice-test-8/math2-q27.jpg","sourcePage":50,"acceptedAnswers":["168"]}]}]}
